@startuml Load Change and Re-declare

title The load changes after filing: re-approval, staleness and the re-declare task
caption Target design. Decisions D13, D27, X3, D24, D31, D32, O21. ADR 0005.

autonumber

actor Dispatcher as disp
actor Administrator as admin
actor "Receiver\n(Ukraine)" as rcv
participant "Freedom API" as api
database "Freedom database" as db

== A box moves between vehicles (for example after a breakdown) ==
disp -> api : move box from vehicle A to vehicle B
group one transaction
  api -> db : change the box's allocation
  api -> db : approved manifests of A and B back to Proposed (X3)
end
api --> disp : moved

== Staleness is derived, never set by hand ==
disp -> api : GET declarations for A and B
api -> db : compare each declaration's snapshot with the current load
api --> disp : A and B declarations: **Stale**
note right of api
  Stale also follows: a box replaced, refused or undeliverable;
  a vehicle swapped or withdrawn; a Receiver no longer registered.
  Not stale: bay moves, label reissues, crew or accommodation changes.
  A declaration closed at its border crossing is never compared again.
end note

disp -> api : GET tasks
api --> disp : re-declare tasks for A and B (shown on screen)

== The convoy cannot depart meanwhile ==
note over disp, api
  "Declarations current" is a blocking requirement for departure.
end note

== Re-approve and re-declare ==
admin -> api : approve A and B again
loop for each stale declaration
  disp -> api : withdraw declaration
  api -> db : Withdrawn (record and old reference kept)\nnew Draft for the same scope
  alt GMR
    disp -> api : update or recreate, then record the reference
  else ENS
    disp -> api : invalidate and refile; record the new MRN (old MRN kept)
  else ELO
    disp -> api : new envelope against the new MRN
  else Ukrainian goods list
    disp -> api : prepare a new goods list
    disp -> rcv : send it for re-filing
    rcv --> disp : new unique code
    disp -> api : record the new reference
    note right
      If the goods are already near the border, they are held at a
      registered hub there until the new filing is accepted (D24, D32).
    end note
  end
end
api --> disp : tasks cleared

@enduml
